<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>paper-trends</title>
{% if inline_css %}<style>{{ inline_css }}</style>{% else %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="report.css">{% endif %}
</head>
<body>
{% if not embedded %}<nav class="masthead"><div class="row"><a class="brand" href="index.html">paper-trends</a></div></nav>{% endif %}
<main class="page{{ ' embedded' if embedded else '' }}">
<header class="title">
  <div class="kicker">{{ tagline }}</div>
  <h1>What a field talks about, year by year</h1>
  <div class="meta"><span>Every paper of a conference from OpenAlex, read as rising and fading phrases, topic shifts and who publishes. Any conference indexed by OpenAlex gets the same page; these are the ones generated ahead of time.</span></div>
</header>
<div class="groups">
{% for group, items in nav %}
<section class="group">
  <h2>{{ group }}</h2>
  <ul class="glance">
  {% for slug, short, name, n in items %}<li><a href="{{ slug ~ '.html' }}"><em>{{ short }}</em> — {{ name }}</a> <span class="n">{{ "{:,}".format(n) }} papers</span></li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
{% endfor %}
</div>
<section>
  <h2>Your own conference</h2>
  <p class="lede">Two commands give any conference indexed by OpenAlex a page like these:</p>
  <pre class="code">uv run python -m paper_trends fetch "Design Automation Conference" --doi-prefix 10.1109/dac --years 2016-2026 --name dac
uv run python -m paper_trends report data/dac.jsonl --years 2016-2025 --out site</pre>
  <p class="lede">For live exploration — pick a term, see the papers behind it, compare venues — run the interactive app: <span class="mono">uv run streamlit run app.py</span>. Source and instructions: <a href="https://github.com/Minjia-Hu/paper-trends">github.com/Minjia-Hu/paper-trends</a>.</p>
</section>
</main>
</body>
</html>
